  _pageType: 0
  _text: 'I climbed a few rungs on the ladder at work, becoming head accountant in
    a larger company. It paid well, and I was able to save up for family holidays:
    the seaside in summer, the mountains in winter. On the side, I gardened and played
    cards with friends on Friday evenings. A stable, unpretentious life.'
